  "summary": "Landin's abstract language from 'The Next 700 Programming Languages' (1966): lambda calculus sugared with let/where, an off-side layout rule and imperative extensions (the J operator), defined via the SECD machine. It is the ancestor of ML, Haskell and Felleisen's ISWIM calculi.",
